# NablaMimic: backpropagation through the simulator over 64-step windows that start from replayed states (a data
# collector fills a replay of 1000 x 4096 states, 2.5 collector steps per update); PODS-style action targets (8
# regression steps toward a + eta dJ/da, RMS setpoint step 0.03 rad annealed to 0.3x with the learning rate); per-sample
# action-gradient clipping at 3x the batch median; TD(lambda) critic on the state each transition starts from;
# termination penalty; SuperMimic-style reset sampling over 1 s bins; the anchor orientation into the decoder, the
# motion encoder hoisted out of the window. The including file chooses the simulator and the action space: absolute
# (setpoints around the default pose) unless it adds --residual-action (configs/ours.args, ours_mjw.args, bones.args).
--seed 0 --clips all --num-envs 4096 --horizon 64 --solver-iterations 10 --no-remat
--reset-sampling supermimic --uniform-over bins
--replay-steps 1000 --collect-envs 4096 --collect-noise 0.1 --utd 0.4
--mask-after-done --critic-pre-state --term-penalty 2 0.08 0.10
--act-noise 0.05 --act-cot-clip 3
--action-target 8 1 0.03 --action-target-lr 6e-4 --action-target-delta-floor 0.3
--anchor-to-decoder --enc-hoist on
--lr 2e-4 --iters 400000 --lr-warmup-steps 500 --lr-decay-to 0.1 --lr-decay-steps 16000
--ckpt-every 250
